      "writtenOn": "2021-04-01T05:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I am aware of the difference. I actually thought that R !\u003d 30 in Java is against the intuition and is one of the major sources of mistake (see the recent announcement from omakoto@). At the source code level, people (even in Java) have been using codename as in `@EnabledSince(targetSdkVersion \u003d Build.VERSION_CODES.R)`. I wish that the preview SDKs have pesudo code names like \"R_preview1\", \"R_preview2\", etc, which translates to \"R\", not 29 or 30, when used in the aapt rule.\n\nAnyway, fixing that is not my immediate goal and this CL doesn\u0027t do that.",
      "parentUuid": "fe21d22b_f924f279",
      "revId": "b37db3686c04d168671333b58c8713607c2bbe35",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
